{{Top}}
{{Quote|We need more firepower! Send in the walkers!|[[Jedi General]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], during the [[second battle of Christophsis]]|<ref name="Disciple">''[[Dark Disciple]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Various_Imperial_walkers.png|thumb|right|300px|Several models of walkers used by the Galactic Empire]]
'''Walkers''' were [[armored cavalry]] [[Ground assault vehicle|vehicles]] that moved on mechanical [[Limb|legs]],<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> often deployed for combat, excavation or scout purposes across a variation of terrain.<ref name="SW EOSAOV (SE)">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles (second edition)]]''</ref> They could possess any number of legs between two<ref name="DB AT-RT">{{Databank|at-rt-walker|AT-RT walker}}</ref> and twelve.<ref name="DB SPHA-T">{{Databank|self-propelled-heavy-artillery-turbolaser-spha-t|Self-Propelled Heavy Artillery Turbolaser (SPHA-T)}}</ref> They were utilized by the [[Galactic Republic]],<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> the [[Galactic Empire]], the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]],<ref name="Commander">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref> the [[New Republic]], [[Imperial Remnants]] including [[Imperial territory G5-623]],<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> [[Visler Korda's faction]],<ref name="Hare-Brained Heist">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|annual=2019|story=Hare-Brained Heist}}</ref> and the [[First Order]].<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

==Skara Nal Mech==
{{Main|Skara Nal Mech}}
An ancient walker and a [[superweapon]] created by the culture of the [[Ancients (Skara Nal)|Ancients]] eons before the founding of the [[Jedi Order]] was a massive, four-legged vehicle, armed with a head-mounted energy weapon capable of significant amounts of destruction.<ref name="Entombed">{{TBB|Entombed}}</ref>

==Galactic Republic walkers==
===Rothana experimental walker===
{{Main|Rothana experimental walker}}
The [[Rothana experimental walker]] was showcased during the [[Valo Republic Fair]].<ref name="The Rising Storm">''[[The High Republic: The Rising Storm]]''</ref>

===All Terrain Attack Pod===
{{Main|All Terrain Attack Pod}}
The All Terrain Attack Pod (AT-AP) was a three-legged walker initially used by the [[Galactic Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref> They were later used by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]] against the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Commander" />

===All Terrain Tactical Enforcer===
{{Main|All Terrain Tactical Enforcer}}
The All Terrain Tactical Enforcer (AT-TE) was a hexapodal walker used by the Galactic Republic during the Clone Wars. The walker had six [[laser cannon]] turrets, a heavy projectile [[mass-driver cannon]], and legs that could be magnetized to climb up and down walls.<ref name="DB AT-TE">{{Databank|at-te-walker|AT-TE Walker}}</ref><ref name="Galactic Defense">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Defense]]''</ref>

===All Terrain Reconnaissance Transport===
{{Main|All Terrain Reconnaissance Transport}}
The All Terrain Reconnaissance Transport (AT-RT) was a small bipedal walker used by the Galactic Republic during the Clone Wars. The walker had an open cockpit, and a single chin-mounted laser cannon. Two of these could be stored in the back of an AT-TE. They were also used by the Empire, the Rebel Alliance, and the First Order.

===All Terrain Open Transport===
{{Main|All Terrain Open Transport}}
The All Terrain Open Transport (AT-OT) was an octapodal walker used by the Galactic Republic toward the end of the Clone Wars.<ref name="ROTS" /> Its open top allowed it to transport more troopers across the battlefield.<ref name="Galactic Defense" />

===Self-Propelled Heavy Artillery Turbolaser===
{{Main|Self-Propelled Heavy Artillery}}
The Self-Propelled Heavy Artillery Turbolaser (SPHA-T)<ref name="DB SPHA-T" /> was a twelve-legged artillery walker used during the start of the Clone Wars.<ref name="AOTC" />

===All Terrain Heavy Enforcer===
{{Main|All Terrain Heavy Enforcer}}
The [[All Terrain Heavy Enforcer]] existed in the time following the AT-TE.<ref name="Complete Vehicles 2018">[[Star Wars: Complete Vehicles (2018)|''Star Wars: Complete Vehicles'' (2018)]]</ref>

